# 16:9 output that follows the game's own Options > Aspect setting.
#
# The game already has a widescreen mode (VisualSettings::mIsWidescreen): a
# 1.666 projection instead of 1.25, widescreen camera zoom data, no letterbox
# bars in cutscenes, and the *wide.thp movies. On hardware it rendered that
# into the usual 4:3 EFB and left the TV to stretch it. BeginFrameTask now
# hands the setting to the host once a frame (osHostSyncWidescreen), which
# locks Aurora's output to 16:9 or 4:3 to match. Aurora scales the logical
# EFB onto the render target, so the stretch happens there. A forced
# --aspect on the command line comes back as the return value and is
# written into the setting, so the camera and projection agree with it.
#
# The full-screen viewport, scissor and copy-source helpers used the render
# size, which only matched the logical EFB while the two had the same shape.
# They now use the EFB size the game configured (glplatGetEFBSize).
